Major finding. `api.sumup.com/authorize` is a **live OAuth authorization gateway** (legacy path not previously enumerated). Key observations:
- It validates `client_id` and `response_type` server-side, requires response_type=code.
- It enforces an allowlist of registered redirect_uris (error surfaced on auth.sumup.com error page).
- **Critical header on ALL responses: `access-control-allow-origin: *`** with `access-control-allow-methods: GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE` and `access-control-max-age: 300`. This is a wildcard CORS header on the OAuth authorization endpoint.
- The `x-envoy-decorator-operation` leaks internal service name `apigateway2-headless.identity.svc.cluster.local:8080/*` (this is a banner leak class — already REJECTED in prior cycles per knowledge).

